{
 "about": "The reverb of the effect rack of the Audio Unit (FXReverb, an item of type 6) on samples of ours played by its noise oscillator (one-shot, 44.1 kHz, rendered at 44.1 kHz), a tone of 25 Hz at 1e-4 under each from its start: in a silence the reverb sleeps, and woken by the signal alone it answers otherwise. Its plain params: kParamType (kHall, kVintage, kSpace, kAbyss; none: the first type), kParamSize 0..100, kParamDelay (the decay) 0..250, kParamFreq (the damping of the lows) and kParamFreqB (of the highs) 0..100, kParamPreDelay (s), kParamWidth, kParamFeedback, kParamLevelOut 0..1, kParamWet 0..100; one not written is at its default (Hall: Size about 35, the decay about 30, FreqB 35, Freq 0, Width 20, LevelOut 0.5). An impulse of 0.5 at 0.3 s, all wet, a measure of it: rt60 (s) of the octaves `octaves` (the fall of the energy left from -5 to -25 dB, from 0.1 s after the impulse, times 3: of 9 s, so a decay over about 12 s is cut short), energy (dB, all of the response against the dry impulse, over 40 Hz), first (ms, the first sample over 2 % of its peak), echo (ms, the first sample over a quarter of its peak from 2 ms on: the first echo after the direct sound), levels (dB against the dry impulse, 50 ms from each of `levelTimes` s), side (dB against the mid, 0.2..1 s). types: every type at its defaults. hall: the Hall at its defaults, echoes [ms, left, right] (the first samples over a quarter of the peak, against the dry impulse: the lines of the Hall are a sixth of an octave apart, left and right in turn), density [s, the share of the samples of 20 ms over their standard deviation against that of a noise]. size, decay, lowDamp, highDamp, predelay, width, feedback, level: the Hall by one param. cross: by two. wet: [Wet, the gain of the dry signal, of the wet one, the rest in dB] of a render at Wet as the sum of those at 0 and 100: the wet gain is s = sin²(Wet/100 · π/2), the dry one 1 - s². scenes: a chord of saws (`chord`: the notes in Hz, each the sum of its harmonics under 16 kHz at 0.12 / h, sines from t = 0, a gate from 0.2 s (5 ms up) to 2.03 s (30 ms down), 6 s) through the Hall at {size, wet}, rows of the windows of 4096 samples around `sceneTimes` s: [level (dB of the mean square of both channels, the sample at full scale 0 dB), the share of each of 25 third octaves from 50 Hz in the spectrum of the mid (Hann, bins from 43 Hz), dB]; dry: the same of the empty rack. scripts/renders/run.mjs --only=reverb",
